WEBVTT

1
00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:14.750
Hi. My name is Peter Parker.

2
00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:19.667
You don't remember me.
but I have something to tell you...

3
00:01:19.917 --> 00:01:21.833
that's gonna sound crazy.

4
00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:25.833
But it's the truth.

5
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.500
And I know you're gonna believe me...

6
00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:32.750
because you're very good
at telling when I'm lying.

7
00:01:34.583 --> 00:01:36.917
E.V.. can you check the calibration
of my targeting matrix?

8
00:01:37.083 --> 00:01:38.667
That doesn't feel zeroed in to me.

9
00:01:38.833 --> 00:01:40.833
Checking target calibration.

10
00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:50.833
Hey. E.V.. take five.

11
00:01:51.583 --> 00:01:52.583
Standing by.

12
00:01:58.333 --> 00:01:59.750
We used to know each other.

13
00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:02.917
We were together.

14
00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:05.667
But something bad was gonna happen...

15
00:02:05.833 --> 00:02:09.333
and the only way to stop it
was to make everyone forget me

16
00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:16.417
First day at MIT. let's go!

17
00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:18.750
Oh. my gosh! We're here! We made it!

18
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:20.500
MJ. come on.

19
00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:21.667
Including you.

20
00:02:21.833 --> 00:02:23.083
Pretend like you're not the happiest
you've ever been...

21
00:02:23.333 --> 00:02:24.667
in your entire life right now.

22
00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:26.583
I can't.

23
00:02:26.833 --> 00:02:29.500
-Let's just do this! You're happy!
-Okay. okay. okay. Okay.

24
00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:31.667
Because I'm not just Peter Parker.

25
00:02:33.417 --> 00:02:34.667
I'm Spider-Man.

26
00:02:34.833 --> 00:02:38.000
I'm really. really understanding the culture
out here in Boston is just so different.

27
00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:40.917
And sometimes
Spider-Man has to do the hard thing...

28
00:02:41.083 --> 00:02:43.000
even if it breaks Peter Parker's heart.

29
00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:46.333
And everyone here is like.
"Pahk the cah by the hahba."

30
00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:49.583
And maybe that's my responsibility.

31
00:02:50.833 --> 00:02:52.250
To live alone with the truth.

32
00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:57.250
But the truth is. MJ. that I love you.

33
00:02:58.750 --> 00:02:59.750
And I hope that deep down...

34
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.583
something inside of you
remembers that you love me. too.

35
00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.667
Suspect is 5'8". 5'10". medium build.

36
00:03:06.833 --> 00:03:09.583
But until then. I'm just gonna be Spider-Man.

37
00:03:15.583 --> 00:03:16.667
Incoming!

38
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.000
Hey. get him!

39
00:03:22.417 --> 00:03:23.750
Hey. hey. hey. Whoa. whoa. whoa!

40
00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.667
Members of the Manfredi crime syndicate...

41
00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:40.333
were apprehended by Spider-Man yesterday.

42
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.750
Hey. we live on the same floor.

43
00:04:04.833 --> 00:04:05.750
Cool.

44
00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.000
Does anybody ever come up here?

45
00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:13.750
Not unless they like asbestos.

46
00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:17.000
We've just been using it for storage.

47
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.417
It's perfect.

48
00:04:20.917 --> 00:04:23.417
Hey. everyone. sophomore-year-Ned is back.

49
00:04:23.917 --> 00:04:26.667
Older. wiser. flyer.

50
00:04:27.917 --> 00:04:28.750
Let's go!

51
00:04:29.583 --> 00:04:32.000
-What is on your face?
Little Caesars -How do you feel about it?

52
00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:34.083
I mean. you look
like an assistant coach.

53
00:04:34.333 --> 00:04:35.250
Huh.

54
00:04:38.833 --> 00:04:40.583
You sure you wanna do this. Scorpion?

55
00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.167
Did you miss me. Spidey?

56
00:04:48.333 --> 00:04:49.500
If I drop you from here...

57
00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:52.000
how long you think
it will take you to hit the ground?

58
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.417
Well. I don't know. You tell me.

59
00:04:55.833 --> 00:04:57.000
Let's end this on a high note. huh?

60
00:05:03.333 --> 00:05:04.417
Yo. Lonnie!

61
00:05:05.083 --> 00:05:06.083
Wha ha happened?

62
00:05:06.333 --> 00:05:09.750
DeWolff. all the evidence you're gonna need
is in the trunk of his car.

63
00:05:09.917 --> 00:05:11.917
You tryin' to take my job. Spider-Man?

64
00:05:12.167 --> 00:05:14.417
Hey. you guys are the professionals.
I'm just a volunteer.

65
00:05:24.917 --> 00:05:26.917
It's a new New York.

66
00:05:27.083 --> 00:05:30.583
Thanks to Spider-Man.
crime rates have dropped to a record low.

67
00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:32.917
Police and Damage Control
give much of the credit...

68
00:05:33.083 --> 00:05:34.083
to the masked hero.

69
00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.500
Initiate HUD test.

70
00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:37.500
Armed robbery at Civic Union Bank.

71
00:05:37.667 --> 00:05:39.667
In the past six months.
he has taken down...

72
00:05:39.833 --> 00:05:42.667
every major crime lord
across the five boroughs...

73
00:05:42.917 --> 00:05:46.333
including the superpowered
ninja group The Hand.

74
00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:52.417
He is the pride of New York City.

75
00:05:52.583 --> 00:05:56.167
The hero every grown-up relies on
and every kid wants to be.

76
00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.500
Final semester. MIT.

77
00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.000
Oh. my gosh. we're graduating in a month.

78
00:06:02.417 --> 00:06:05.667
We've made so many memories.
Where do I begin?

79
00:06:05.833 --> 00:06:08.750
Night swimming in the Charles River
with Jim and Wiley.

80
00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.667
The infamous food fun at the Banana Lounge.

81
00:06:11.917 --> 00:06:16.083
Pulling all-nighters in Stud 5
with MJ and Nate Dawg.

82
00:06:16.333 --> 00:06:19.000
It feels like yesterday
I was sitting on a roof with MJ...

83
00:06:19.167 --> 00:06:22.250
dreaming about coming here together.
and I still can't believe we did it.

84
00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:25.000
I'm so grateful
for all the friends that I've made.

85
00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.500
I couldn't imagine
going through this with anyone else.

86
00:06:27.667 --> 00:06:29.500
Ned. who do you think
is actually watching these?

87
00:06:29.833 --> 00:06:32.167
-I don't know. But maybe someone.
-Okay.

88
00:06:32.417 --> 00:06:33.500
Okay. well. bye. someone.

89
00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.833
-What? No!
-Bye. We're done. Yeah. we're done.

90
00:06:46.333 --> 00:06:48.250
Leave it outside the door.

91
00:06:53.417 --> 00:06:56.500
I mean. we're talking about downtown Brooklyn. in broad daylight.

92
00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:58.167
High profile job like that.

93
00:06:58.267 --> 00:06:59.417
you know that Foswell was involved.

94
00:06:59.667 --> 00:07:01.750
Yeah. I hear you. but can you prove it?

95
00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:03.667
Yeah. I'm going through
his financial records...

96
00:07:03.917 --> 00:07:05.333
and I'm following his crew every night.

97
00:07:06.333 --> 00:07:08.250
Do you do anything besides work?

98
00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:09.917
You know the saying.
"You do something you love...

99
00:07:10.083 --> 00:07:11.333
you don't work a day in your life."

100
00:07:12.917 --> 00:07:14.833
-Mom. where's my calculator?
-I don't know.

101
00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:18.750
Trust me. aight?
Being married to the job never ends well.

102
00:07:19.083 --> 00:07:20.917
Well. don't worry about it. I'll be okay.

103
00:07:21.167 --> 00:07:23.750
Oh. yeah?
You still getting them headaches. though?

104
00:07:25.167 --> 00:07:27.500
Yeah. But I'll be fine.

105
00:07:27.667 --> 00:07:28.750
I don't know. man.

106
00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:30.917
I think you're body's tryin'
to tell you somethin'.

107
00:07:31.167 --> 00:07:33.333
Like you need to get outta that suit
every once in a while.

108
00:07:33.583 --> 00:07:35.333
Mom. do you know where my calculator is?

109
00:07:35.583 --> 00:07:36.500
I don't know. Papi.

110
00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.750
What you need is some real human connection.

111
00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.167
What? And we're not connecting?

112
00:07:41.583 --> 00:07:46.250
Nah. dude. I don't know your name.
your face. or nothing about you.

113
00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:48.667
I don't think you've ever asked me a question
about my life.

114
00:07:48.833 --> 00:07:49.833
Sure. I have.

115
00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:51.250
Yeah. what are my kids' names?

116
00:07:51.917 --> 00:07:53.917
Well. for starters. your son's name's Papi.

117
00:07:55.667 --> 00:07:56.583
Is it Spider-Man?

118
00:07:56.833 --> 00:07:58.750
I can't tell you that. sweetheart.

119
00:07:59.167 --> 00:08:00.583
That means it's Spider-Man.

120
00:08:00.833 --> 00:08:01.833
Gosh.

121
00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:07.333
A hijacked tank is heading southbound
past 34th Street.

122
00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:08.917
All available units respond.

123
00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:10.250
Hey. you getting this?

124
00:08:10.417 --> 00:08:12.083
More work. Lucky you.

125
00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:13.250
Okay. I'll see you out there.

126
00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:14.583
I'm so sorry. I gotta go.

127
00:09:31.917 --> 00:09:33.083
I got you. Spidey!

128
00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:34.583
No. no. I don't need your...

129
00:09:48.917 --> 00:09:49.917
Hey! Heads up!

130
00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:54.917
You okay. kid? Yeah. you're okay.
See ya later.

131
00:09:59.583 --> 00:10:00.917
You wouldn't know it just by looking at it...

132
00:10:01.167 --> 00:10:04.167
but this very street was completely destroyed
in the Battle of New York.

133
00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:14.167
Come on. come on. come on.

134
00:10:15.833 --> 00:10:17.667
Come on.

135
00:10:30.667 --> 00:10:31.583
Oh. God.

136
00:10:40.333 --> 00:10:41.333
Come on.

137
00:10:42.167 --> 00:10:42.750
Hey.

138
00:10:44.333 --> 00:10:46.250
The hell. Frank?
You just hit me with the van!

139
00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:47.667
Quit your whimpering.

140
00:10:47.833 --> 00:10:49.167
We're not doing that again. Frank.

141
00:10:49.333 --> 00:10:50.667
You're goddamn right we're not.

142
00:10:50.833 --> 00:10:52.583
This time you're gonna
get the hell outta my way.

143
00:10:53.083 --> 00:10:54.583
You mean. instead of saving your life?

144
00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:57.917
You gonna talk about
that Staten Island bullshit again?

145
00:10:58.167 --> 00:10:59.500
Well. you said it. not me.

146
00:10:59.667 --> 00:11:00.500
Jeez.

147
00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:02.583
Look. man. you can't just shoot yourself
out of every situation.

148
00:11:02.833 --> 00:11:04.083
Innocent people get hurt.

149
00:11:04.333 --> 00:11:06.667
Who do you think's downrange of that tank.
dumb-dumb?

150
00:11:12.167 --> 00:11:13.167
Suit yourself.

151
00:11:16.833 --> 00:11:17.833
Jackass.

152
00:11:18.833 --> 00:11:20.000
This freakin' guy.

153
00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:37.250
Go home. Frank!

154
00:11:41.917 --> 00:11:43.417
I'm gonna kill this kid.

155
00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:50.500
-DeWolff?
-Are you gonna stop that thing or what?

156
00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:53.083
It's heading straight
for the Damage Control Detention Center.

157
00:11:53.333 --> 00:11:54.250
I'm trying.

158
00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:55.333
Try harder.

159
00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:57.167
There's a lot of scary dudes
locked up in there.

160
00:11:57.333 --> 00:11:58.917
Well. who do you think put them in there?

161
00:11:59.833 --> 00:12:03.083
Let's go. Scorpion. Moving day.

162
00:12:33.333 --> 00:12:36.083
All right. everybody. clear out!
This guy is armed and dangerous.

163
00:12:48.333 --> 00:12:49.833
Get out of the vehicle. ma'am.

164
00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.250
I was thinking the same thing.

165
00:13:01.083 --> 00:13:02.500
Spider-Man?

166
00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.000
Where am I?

167
00:13:12.167 --> 00:13:13.250
What?

168
00:13:15.833 --> 00:13:17.250
Move! Move! Move!

169
00:13:17.417 --> 00:13:19.167
Keep her for questioning.
Clear the building.

170
00:13:22.333 --> 00:13:24.333
Enjoy the ride. Scorpion!

171
00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:27.000
You won't be seeing much daylight
in supermax.

172
00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:30.000
Scorpions are nocturnal. buddy.

173
00:13:33.083 --> 00:13:36.250
The building is under attack.
Get the prisoner out of here now!

174
00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:42.417
Sir!

175
00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:02.667
You gotta take off now!

176
00:14:02.833 --> 00:14:04.833
The building has been breached. Go! Go!

177
00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:07.833
Hey. fire it up! Go! Go!

178
00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:17.417
Change of plans!

179
00:14:18.083 --> 00:14:20.000
Take him to the helipad at Bellevue.

180
00:14:20.667 --> 00:14:23.750
-What?
-That's an order from Director Metzger. Go!

181
00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:24.917
Now!

182
00:14:25.167 --> 00:14:26.083
Copy that.

183
00:14:37.083 --> 00:14:38.667
Hey! What...

184
00:14:38.833 --> 00:14:40.250
How did I get up here?

185
00:14:44.583 --> 00:14:47.500
Spider-Man. save me. would you?

186
00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:54.333
Who are you?

187
00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:56.833
You can see me.

188
00:14:57.083 --> 00:14:58.417
Tell me who you are.

189
00:14:59.667 --> 00:15:00.583
You first.

190
00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:05.833
Hey. Hey.

191
00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:13.000
You pushed me out.

192
00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:14.750
Interesting.

193
00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:16.333
What the hell was that?

194
00:15:16.583 --> 00:15:18.667
Did you just try to jump into my mind?

195
00:15:18.833 --> 00:15:21.750
You know. the whole time
you've been chasing me...

196
00:15:22.583 --> 00:15:25.167
you forgot to ask yourself
a very important question.

197
00:15:27.083 --> 00:15:28.417
What's in the tank?

198
00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:31.917
Go! Move.

199
00:15:46.083 --> 00:15:47.083
Spider-Man?

200
00:15:48.333 --> 00:15:49.417
What just happened?

201
00:15:52.417 --> 00:15:53.417
I don't know.

202
00:15:56.833 --> 00:15:57.667
Hey. way to go. Spidey.

203
00:15:57.917 --> 00:15:59.500
You guys okay? You good?

204
00:15:59.667 --> 00:16:02.500
I swear. All the things they said I did.
I don't remember doing any of them.

205
00:16:02.667 --> 00:16:04.667
It's okay. it's okay.
Look. let these people take good care of you.

206
00:16:04.917 --> 00:16:05.667
I would never hurt you.

207
00:16:06.083 --> 00:16:06.917
-Okay.
-I love you. Spider-Man

208
00:16:07.417 --> 00:16:08.750
Yeah. All right. buddy. All right.

209
00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:10.917
-Hey. what do you got?
-Here. get this.

210
00:16:11.167 --> 00:16:12.667
Chopper took Scorpion to Bellevue.

211
00:16:12.917 --> 00:16:15.083
Ten minutes later.
a guard walked him right out the door.

212
00:16:15.667 --> 00:16:16.250
What?

213
00:16:16.667 --> 00:16:17.583
What about the tank?

214
00:16:17.833 --> 00:16:20.333
Stolen from the Damage Control
warehouse in Brooklyn.

215
00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:22.583
Driver was a janitor who worked there.

216
00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:23.667
You got a motive?

217
00:16:23.917 --> 00:16:24.667
Nada.

218
00:16:24.917 --> 00:16:25.917
And no criminal record.

219
00:16:26.083 --> 00:16:28.083
Scorpion must've gotten to her somehow.

220
00:16:29.167 --> 00:16:30.250
Yeah. Maybe.

221
00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:32.417
What do you mean. "maybe"?

222
00:16:32.917 --> 00:16:34.500
I mean. I don't know.

223
00:16:35.333 --> 00:16:36.500
But I know someone that might.

224
00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:37.667
Where you going?

225
00:16:37.917 --> 00:16:39.417
You keep following the leads on Scorpion.

226
00:16:39.667 --> 00:16:41.333
I'm gonna go talk to someone.

227
00:16:56.833 --> 00:17:00.333
Hi. is this 3250 Brighton Beach?

228
00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:06.083
Okay.

229
00:17:06.833 --> 00:17:08.583
I think I know what that means.

230
00:17:13.667 --> 00:17:14.833
Take off your clothes.

231
00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:18.917
What?

232
00:17:19.417 --> 00:17:21.333
You don't wear clothes in the banya.

233
00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:23.833
Ditch the leotard.

234
00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:26.333
This is not a leotard.

235
00:17:27.167 --> 00:17:29.083
Your text said that this was your office.

236
00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:32.000
This is my office.

237
00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:33.750
Get in.

238
00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.417
I'm fine. thanks. I'll just...

239
00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:39.083
My office. my rules.

240
00:17:39.333 --> 00:17:42.917
This way you get to enjoy
a nice. relaxing soak.

241
00:17:43.167 --> 00:17:45.333
and I get to see that
you don't have any weapons...

242
00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:46.667
and we both win.

243
00:17:48.917 --> 00:17:49.917
Okay.

244
00:17:59.167 --> 00:18:01.500
Really? What. you never take that off?

245
00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:03.833
No. I... You know. it defeats
the whole anonymous thing.

246
00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:08.417
Even for your girlfriend
or boyfriend or whatever?

247
00:18:09.167 --> 00:18:10.750
There's a lot of conjecture online.

248
00:18:11.583 --> 00:18:14.167
And super graphic artwork. Have you seen?

249
00:18:14.333 --> 00:18:16.917
The one with you
and the ten Mysterios. it's...

250
00:18:17.083 --> 00:18:19.250
I've seen it. I've...

251
00:18:19.417 --> 00:18:20.750
It's hard to unsee. to be honest.

252
00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:23.000
But. look. I don't have anyone.
I just kinda keep to myself.

253
00:18:23.833 --> 00:18:25.333
All by yourself? All the time?

254
00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:26.833
No wonder you're so sad.

255
00:18:27.083 --> 00:18:29.083
-I'm not so sad.
-A little bit.

256
00:18:29.333 --> 00:18:31.167
Could we just talk about
what I came here to talk to you about...

257
